  "body": "**Bump egui, egui-winit and egui-wgpu from 0.36.2 to 0.37** (and wgpu to the matching version), so CamCraft's UI can share SolidCraft's UI crates.\n\n**Why:** SolidCraft (tangency-labs/solidcraft, 0.40.0-rc) builds on `egui 0.37`, `eframe 0.37`, `egui-wgpu 0.37` (vendored) and `wgpu 30`. CamCraft pins `=0.36.2`. Two egui versions in one binary can't share types, so no SolidCraft crate (`solidcraft-theme`, `solidcraft-color` or the coming `solidcraft-ui-kit`) can be pinned until CamCraft is on 0.37. This is a prerequisite of #655.\n\n**Done means:** the workspace builds on egui 0.37 with clippy clean. The ui suites and the structural tests (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/structural.rs`) pass, and any API break is fixed in place. Snapshot PNGs aren't refreshed here; the cut does that (AGENTS.md). The `gpu_select` / `gpu_init` paths are re-checked on macOS Metal.\n\nPart of #655\n",
